rticle_WYSIWYG__O0uhw article_articlePage__UMz3q text-[18px] leading-8 arti=
cle_revampLinks__mNkFw"><div><p>Bumrungrad Hospital Public Company Limited =
reported mixed second-quarter 2026 results, with earnings per share of $2.1=
8 coming in below the $2.28 forecast, while revenue reached $6.28 billion, =
above the $6.10 billion estimate. The stock rose 0.53% to $191 after the re=
port and was last trading at $198, up 1.02% from the previous close, leavin=
g it near the top of its 52-week range of $136 to $214.</p>
<p></p><h2><b>Key Takeaways</b></h2><p></p><ul><li>Revenue rose 2.9% year o=
ver year in Q2, supported by stronger international demand.</li><li>EPS mis=
sed forecasts by about 4.4%, but revenue beat expectations by about 3.0%.</=
li><li>EBITDA margin held at 41.4%, while net profit margin was 30.1%.</li>=
<li>Non-Thai patient revenue increased 7.1%, offsetting a 2.2% decline in T=
hai patient revenue.</li><li>The board approved an interim dividend of THB =
4 per share, double the historical THB 2.</li></ul><p></p><h2><b>Company Pe=
rformance</b></h2><p>Bumrungrad said it delivered solid results in Q2 and f=
or the first half of 2026, despite weakness in the Thai domestic market and=
 continued pressure from Cambodia. Total revenue in the quarter was THB 6,2=
78 million, up 2.9% from a year earlier, while hospital operations revenue =
rose 3.8%.</p>
<p>The company=E2=80=99s international business remained the main growth en=
gine. Non-Thai patient revenue increased 7.1% in the quarter and 5.6% in th=
e first half. Management said Middle East, Myanmar and U.S. patients helped=
 offset softer Thai demand.</p>
<p>Profitability remained strong by industry standards. EBITDA rose 2.4% ye=
ar over year to THB 2,599 million, and net profit increased 1.7% to THB 1,8=
89 million. The company=E2=80=99s EBITDA margin was 41.4%, and its net prof=
it margin was 30.1%.</p><div><div class=3D"flex flex-col gap-3 leading-norm=
